  "Monitor, owner-delegated (2026-10-16, relayed by the lane monitor, verbatim): Q-HE4B-0 (a): HE-004B1 first; B2 per Q-HE4B-11. Q-HE4B-1 (a): check_qualification and the acceptance token in HE-004D, bound to the record digest. Q-HE4B-2 (c): test-side localisation with the existing is_valid, plus the listed prefix fallback. Q-HE4B-4 (a): embedded digest-pinned bytes only. Q-HE4B-5 (a): two private literals as exact expressions. Q-HE4B-7 (a): the next operator edge record supersedes the current one by sha256, carries B1's 10 rows with full commits, and is published by W03-PLAN-AMEND-2. Include the I05-v4 rows in the same record if they are ready by then. Q-HE4B-8 (a): B compares and defines the record; C parses and supplies the pinned hash; HE-008 binds by digest. Q-HE4B-9 (a): closed request specs with completeness checks; the shared NotServed input (MutatingAdmissionPolicy kinds only); metadata-only OR05 lists; quota headroom goes to C. Q-HE4B-10 (a)+(c): production returns Unavailable without touching the fixture path; the v2 halves of X02–X04 are replayed. Q-HE4B-11 (b): fold B2 into HE-004D after native-profile v4 and the I06 successor, and split D so its v4-only captures aren't held. Q-HE4-5 and Q-HE4-6 are decided with C; Q-HE4-7 and Q-HE4-8 go through Q-HE4B-10/11 and Q-HE4B-7 as listed.",
  "Monitor, owner-delegated (2026-10-16, relayed by the lane monitor, verbatim): Agreed: one operator edge record carrying the I05 v4 rows and HE-004B1's 10 rows, published by W03-PLAN-AMEND-2.",
  "Monitor, owner-delegated (2026-10-16, relayed by the lane monitor, verbatim): 1. Packet names: - HE-004B1, HE-004C, HE-004D1, HE-004D2 and HE-004-I01 are accepted. - The I05-v4 adoption is HE-003A3, since it continues the I05 gate-channel family after HE-003A and HE-003A2. If an R10 convention says otherwise, propose it at the contract review."
